                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_595">Winchester, Hampshire. College
                        of St Mary the Virgin of Winchester. </orgName><p>Flyleaves of this bursars'
                        account book for the years 1583--99 are four folios from a 14th-cent.
                        English copy of Iacobus de Voragine's Legenda aurea (containing parts of the
                        Lives of St Clement I and St Catharine).There may be a presumption that the
                        scrap for these flyleaves was sourced locally, and indeed may well belong to
                        the copy given to the library by the fellow Nicholas North (d. 1445) and
                        reported in the inventory in the Liber Albus, fol. 34v.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Nicholas North (d. 1445), fellow of
